        "id": 1108919
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-06-29T18:25:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "help me understand why we embed the profile information in the mime/mediatype\nfor these, yet for things like AAC audio, the profile information handled separately.\n\nthis feels like it leads to having many separate\nif (its DTSHD_PROFILE1 || DTSHD_PROFILE2 || ....) { ...}\ninstead of\nif (its DTSHD) {  and we handle profiles within the DTSHD specific code }\n\nthis puts the profile determination into the DTSHD codecs.\nas written, if we want to add a DTSHD_PROFILE3, we have to modify the framework.\n\nI\u0027m in agreement with the MIMETYPE_AUDIO_VND_DTSHD, but i\u0027m questioning the 4 entries that have PROFILE in their name.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21472,
        "startChar": 55,
        "endLine": 21472,
        "endChar": 75
      },
      "revId": "643d6f08e7bf47c2972b89f72ca38b9b645d9ac6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d789132f_eb8df60e",
        "filename": "core/api/current.txt",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 21472,
      "author": {
        "id": 1938941
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-06-30T18:30:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for providing the suggestion.\n\nIt may be required to handle the \u0027DTSHD\u0027, \u0027DTSHD_PROFILE_LBR\u0027 and \u0027DTSHD_PROFILE_MA\u0027 differently.\nThe audio decoding devices which only have the legacy \u0027DTS Digital Surround\u0027 capability can\u0027t handle the LBR or MA type streams.\nBut those devices can decode the \u0027DTSHD\u0027 type streams(by discarding unknown bitstream construct in HD streams).\n\nSimilarly, the \u0027DTSUHD_PROFILE_P1\u0027 decoder can\u0027t handle the \u0027DTSUHD_PROFILE_P2\u0027 type streams.\n\nPlease note that, the Profile1, and Profile 2 extensions are used with \u0027DTS UHD\u0027 stream category not with the \u0027DTS HD\u0027.",
      "parentUuid": "73b78d0d_fad83ded",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21472,
        "startChar": 55,
        "endLine": 21472,
        "endChar": 75
      },
      "revId": "643d6f08e7bf47c2972b89f72ca38b9b645d9ac6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ed55e93c_a6757a63",
        "filename": "core/api/current.txt",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 21472,
      "author": {
        "id": 1108919
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-13T18:19:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "https://www.iana.org/assignments/media-types/audio/vnd.dts.hd\nseems to indicate that\nthe \";profile\u003d\" is a required part of the mimetype.  ok that means that\ncontent exists and will show up with this...\n\nthe \";profile\u003d\" piece is marked as a required parameter; I wish we had a better way to encode that parameter.\n\nThe web page above does seem to say that\n\u003d\u003d MIMETYPE_AUDIO_VND_DTSHD \u003d \"audio/vnd.dts.hd\";\nis invalid, since the \"profile\u003d\" is listed as a required parameter.\n\nif we\u0027re going to accept \"audio/vnd.dts.hd\" even though it\u0027s not compliant (e.g. because we want to be forgiving about bad content). then we should probably do something like immediately convert that invalid mimetype string into a legal one (meaning add a \u0027;profile\u003dxxx\u0027) so that we can do all of the rest of the processing with just the legal sets of profiles.",
      "parentUuid": "d789132f_eb8df60e",
